Procurement Policy

    This policy defines the rules that must be followed
when purchasing goods or services for the company.

    Every purchase must have a valid business purpose.
The requesting department must have enough available
budget, and the selected quotation must not exceed the
maximum budget defined in the purchase request.

    Purchases above €5,000 require at least two supplier
quotations. Purchases above €15,000 require at least
three supplier quotations.

    The selected supplier must be able to provide the
requested product and quantity and should meet the
required delivery deadline.

    Suppliers should be compared based on total price,
delivery time, warranty, supplier approval status,
requested quantity, and the requirements of the purchase request.

    The cheapest supplier should not automatically be
selected if another supplier better satisfies the purchase
requirements.

    A purchase must not proceed if the selected quotation
exceeds the department's available budget.

    Supplier quotations and the procurement recommendation
must be available before final approval.
